            "result_text": "I've created the regex and saved it to `/app/regex.txt`. Here's how it works:\n\n**Key components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 validation** - Matches 4 octets (0-255) separated by dots: `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|[01]?[0-9][0-9]?)`\n\n2. **Date patterns with month-day validation**:\n   - 31-day months (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): days 01-31\n   - 30-day months (04,06,09,11): days 01-30  \n   - February: days 01-29 (as required)\n\n3. **Word boundaries** - Uses `(?<![0-9a-zA-Z])` and `(?![0-9a-zA-Z])` to ensure valid dates and IPs aren't preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters\n\n4. **Last date only** - Uses `(?=.*IPv4_PATTERN)` to verify IPv4 exists, then `.*?` with a negative lookahead `(?!.*DATE_PATTERN)` to ensure only the last date on the line is captured\n\nThe regex returns the captured date through the single capturing group, so `re.findall()` will return just the dates without extra groups."
